{
  "dom_id": "step-q328577",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.68).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9515\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ | $\\,0.9535\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9608\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ | $\\,0.9625\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.9686\\,$ | $\\,0.9693\\,$ | $\\,0.9699\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.68)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<1.68)=P(Z\\le 1.68)=Φ(1.68).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/244c5a3af574c72e499c5e2dd14c81e3d202b903300344b85e42e4bf5129f0c7.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(1.68)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $1.6$ and the column that corresponds to $0.08.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9515\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ | $\\,0.9535\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9608\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ | $\\,0.9625\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.9686\\,$ | $\\,0.9693\\,$ | $\\,0.9699\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.68)=Φ(1.68)=0.9535.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
